WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:02.634
-Guys, it can be hard
to say goodbye,

00:00:02.634 --> 00:00:04.067
but sometimes you have to,
and there are a few things

00:00:04.067 --> 00:00:06.033
I'd like to say goodbye to
right now.

00:00:06.033 --> 00:00:08.734
It's time for "Go On, Git!"

00:00:08.734 --> 00:00:10.334
-♪ Go on, git ♪

00:00:10.334 --> 00:00:12.100
♪ Go on, git ♪

00:00:12.100 --> 00:00:17.200
♪ Go on, go on, go on, git ♪

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:18.767
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:18.767 --> 00:00:21.968
-Go on, git, paper straws.

00:00:21.968 --> 00:00:24.634
I'll tip my hat to what you're
doing for the environment,

00:00:24.634 --> 00:00:26.367
but you got a three-sip maximum

00:00:26.367 --> 00:00:28.467
before you fold
like wet origami.

00:00:28.467 --> 00:00:30.300
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:31.534
Go on, git, paper straws.

00:00:31.534 --> 00:00:33.934
For something you can't suck,
you sure do suck.

00:00:33.934 --> 00:00:37.400
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:37.400 --> 00:00:39.901
[ Spit, clang ]

00:00:39.901 --> 00:00:41.734
-Go on, git...

00:00:41.734 --> 00:00:46.367
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:46.367 --> 00:00:48.734
...true-crime documentaries...

00:00:48.734 --> 00:00:50.501
[ Laughter ]

00:00:50.501 --> 00:00:53.267
...where the mystery
isn't solved at the end.

00:00:53.267 --> 00:00:54.367
[ Laughter ]

00:00:54.367 --> 00:00:56.968
I just binged nine
hour-long episodes,

00:00:56.968 --> 00:00:59.601
and you're telling me
you don't even have a guess

00:00:59.601 --> 00:01:01.567
as to who the killer is?

00:01:01.567 --> 00:01:02.634
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:02.634 --> 00:01:04.968
Well, now I'm just scared.

00:01:04.968 --> 00:01:06.334
[ Laughter ]

00:01:06.334 --> 00:01:10.133
'Cause now there's some
crazy killer on the loose,

00:01:10.133 --> 00:01:13.934
and he knows that I know
everything he did.

00:01:13.934 --> 00:01:15.801
[ Laughter ]

00:01:15.801 --> 00:01:20.167
I'd be a dead man if it wasn't
for my Ring doorbell alarm.

00:01:20.167 --> 00:01:22.701
[ Laughter ]

00:01:22.701 --> 00:01:23.767
Now, go on, git.

00:01:23.767 --> 00:01:30.234
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:30.234 --> 00:01:31.434
-Go on, git...

00:01:31.434 --> 00:01:33.567
[ Laughter ]

00:01:33.567 --> 00:01:35.601
Sorry.
Go on, git.

00:01:35.601 --> 00:01:37.601
It was just going all the way
down my throat, and it was --

00:01:37.601 --> 00:01:39.000
[ Laughter ]

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:43.501
Go on, git, people who say every
firework is their favorite.

00:01:43.501 --> 00:01:46.167
You do know how fireworks shows
are structured, right?

00:01:46.167 --> 00:01:48.667
They get progressively better
as the show goes on.

00:01:48.667 --> 00:01:51.000
They don't start
with the best fireworks.

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:54.000
That's like Train opening their
concert with "Drops of Jupiter."

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:55.567
Ain't gonna happen.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:55.567 --> 00:01:58.033
So go on, "ooh,"
and git, "ahh."

00:01:58.033 --> 00:02:02.934
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:02.934 --> 00:02:07.067
-Go on, git, kidney bean-shaped
swimming pools.

00:02:07.067 --> 00:02:10.033
[ Laughter ]

00:02:10.033 --> 00:02:11.501
What, being a rectangle
ain't good enough for you?

00:02:11.501 --> 00:02:12.767
[ Laughter ]

00:02:12.767 --> 00:02:15.834
A circle not cool enough?

00:02:15.834 --> 00:02:19.734
No, you just get to have
all the attention, don't you?

00:02:19.734 --> 00:02:21.968
And by the way, the human kidney

00:02:21.968 --> 00:02:25.267
is an organ
designed to create urine.

00:02:25.267 --> 00:02:26.634
[ Laughter ]

00:02:26.634 --> 00:02:29.534
And that is the last thing
I want to be thinking about

00:02:29.534 --> 00:02:31.801
before cannonballing
into the deep end.

00:02:31.801 --> 00:02:33.033
[ Laughter ]

00:02:33.033 --> 00:02:37.367
So go on, git,
kidney-shaped swimming pools.

00:02:37.367 --> 00:02:38.434
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:38.434 --> 00:02:40.767
Unless you're in
my neighbor's backyard.

00:02:40.767 --> 00:02:42.067
Then I'm coming over.

00:02:42.067 --> 00:02:46.434
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:46.434 --> 00:02:47.501
-G--

00:02:47.501 --> 00:02:53.534
[ Laughter ]

00:02:53.534 --> 00:02:56.567
-Go on, git...

00:02:56.567 --> 00:02:58.801
screen doors with locks.

00:02:58.801 --> 00:02:59.834
[ Laughter ]

00:02:59.834 --> 00:03:00.968
Let me get this straight.

00:03:00.968 --> 00:03:03.100
You're supposed
to protect my home?

00:03:03.100 --> 00:03:04.801
So if a burglar shows up,
they're gonna be like,

00:03:04.801 --> 00:03:06.734
"They -- they -- they got
a screen door, fellas.

00:03:06.734 --> 00:03:08.701
Pack it in!"
[ Laughter ]

00:03:08.701 --> 00:03:11.834
You're absolutely impenetrable
unless someone has the strength

00:03:11.834 --> 00:03:14.234
to press through a tea bag.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:14.234 --> 00:03:16.968
So, reach in, finger-flick
that tiny little lock

00:03:16.968 --> 00:03:20.167
that doesn't do nothing,
come on in, and then go git.

00:03:20.167 --> 00:03:25.567
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:25.567 --> 00:03:26.901
-Go on, git...

00:03:26.901 --> 00:03:28.400
[ Laughter ]

00:03:28.400 --> 00:03:30.734
...people asking me if I --

00:03:30.734 --> 00:03:32.167
I can hardly talk.
Hold on.

00:03:32.167 --> 00:03:38.567
[ Laughter ]

00:03:38.567 --> 00:03:41.367
That's not chaw.
It's just a wad of napkins.

00:03:41.367 --> 00:03:43.200
[ Laughter ]

00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:44.767
Go on, git, people asking me

00:03:44.767 --> 00:03:47.300
if I have plans
for the Fourth of July.

00:03:47.300 --> 00:03:50.100
If'n I did,
and if'n you were included,

00:03:50.100 --> 00:03:51.901
I'm pretty sure
you'd know by now.

00:03:51.901 --> 00:03:53.133
[ Laughter ]

00:03:53.133 --> 00:03:57.067
So, if I happen to see you
at Dave's barbecue,

00:03:57.067 --> 00:03:59.400
I'd say two things to you --

00:03:59.400 --> 00:04:03.734
"Happy birthday, 'Merica,"
and "Go on, git!"

00:04:03.734 --> 00:04:07.601
-Yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:07.601 --> 00:04:10.667
[ Spit, clang ]

00:04:10.734 --> 00:04:12.868
[ Spit, clang ]

00:04:12.934 --> 00:04:14.901
[ Spit, clang ]

00:04:14.901 --> 00:04:21.100
[ Laughter ]

00:04:21.100 --> 00:04:23.234
[ Spit, clang ]

00:04:23.234 --> 00:04:25.133
[ Laughter ]

00:04:25.133 --> 00:04:28.334
Go on, git,
"My money don't jiggle jiggle."

00:04:28.334 --> 00:04:29.801
You had your time,
but guess what --

00:04:29.801 --> 00:04:32.868
your aunt done ruined it by
posting about it on Facebook.

00:04:32.868 --> 00:04:35.701
It's been real,
but you've tik'd your last tok.

00:04:35.701 --> 00:04:38.200
So take a hike,
"My money don't jiggle jiggle,"

00:04:38.200 --> 00:04:40.567
and say hi to "cheugy"
and "bing bong" on the way out.

00:04:40.567 --> 00:04:42.300
Go on, sheesh!

00:04:42.300 --> 00:04:43.767
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:43.767 --> 00:04:45.000
So hard to see 'em go,

00:04:45.000 --> 00:04:47.033
but I'm glad I got that
all out of my system.

00:04:47.033 --> 00:04:48.901
My thanks to Steve Carell.

00:04:48.901 --> 00:04:50.968
We'll be talking with him
after the break.

